1
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:14,180
MICHIKO DAIMON, FREELANCE SURGEON

2
00:00:14,247 --> 00:00:16,049
Same as me.

3
00:00:16,116 --> 00:00:17,484
That's great.

4
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:20,720
You look so cute.

5
00:00:21,254 --> 00:00:23,623
That's good. That's really good.

6
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:28,528
MAYA KOKONOE, MODEL

7
00:00:28,595 --> 00:00:30,730
Yes, that was really good.

8
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:32,432
Yes...

9
00:00:32,499 --> 00:00:34,200
Touch your hair.

10
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,668
That's good.

11
00:00:35,735 --> 00:00:37,037
Yes, that's right.

12
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:44,344
What's wrong?

13
00:00:48,748 --> 00:00:51,284
Why is she wearing that?

14
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:56,856
I thought these were new.

15
00:00:56,923 --> 00:00:58,391
Maya...

16
00:00:58,458 --> 00:00:59,959
Maya, wait!

17
00:01:00,026 --> 00:01:01,061
Just hold on.

18
00:01:01,127 --> 00:01:02,295
Wait up...

19
00:01:02,362 --> 00:01:03,963
How scary.

20
00:01:11,871 --> 00:01:14,207
- It's your fault.
- Make it up to us!

21
00:01:14,707 --> 00:01:16,943
- How could you?
- Stop right there.

22
00:01:17,377 --> 00:01:20,713
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

23
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:51,778
<i>In 2014, medical establishments collapsed</i>
<i>and became more corrupt.</i>

24
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:52,712
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

25
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:59,619
<i>The Surgical Department Directors</i>
<i>will make their rounds now.</i>

26
00:02:00,987 --> 00:02:03,289
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

27
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:06,960
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

28
00:02:07,827 --> 00:02:10,563
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

29
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:14,734
<i>Japan announced to export</i>
<i>state of the art medical services</i>

30
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:17,303
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

31
00:02:17,904 --> 00:02:22,642
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>
<i>of the strong preying on the weak.</i>

32
00:02:28,381 --> 00:02:29,582
Amazing.

33
00:02:40,727 --> 00:02:42,929
She's pretty.

34
00:02:44,898 --> 00:02:49,302
The Japan Healthcare Organization.
What a fantastic idea.

35
00:02:49,369 --> 00:02:51,905
You've won over the ministries.

36
00:02:51,971 --> 00:02:53,439
Great work.

37
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:55,108
Thank you.

38
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,042
YOSHIHITO TENDO, PRESIDENT

39
00:02:56,442 --> 00:02:58,711
Just one ministry left.

40
00:02:58,778 --> 00:03:02,448
The bill for
the Japan Healthcare Organization

41
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:04,484
depends on the next Minister.

42
00:03:05,151 --> 00:03:07,086
I still can't rest easy.

43
00:03:07,153 --> 00:03:10,390
I'm sure you already have a plan.

44
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:21,134
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

45
00:03:22,669 --> 00:03:26,272
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

46
00:03:34,247 --> 00:03:35,615
So you're a doctor.

47
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:39,586
- What?
- <i>For example, this woman.</i>

48
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:43,690
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

49
00:03:44,290 --> 00:03:48,995
<i>Her medical license and experience</i>
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

50
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:53,132
You could be a model.

51
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:54,033
Thanks.

52
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:55,435
But you're too old.

53
00:04:00,673 --> 00:04:02,008
Want me to treat you?

54
00:04:03,943 --> 00:04:06,045
You have a lumbar problem, right?

55
00:04:14,487 --> 00:04:15,922
Where's Dr. Kaji?

56
00:04:15,989 --> 00:04:18,291
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

57
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:20,627
<i>also known as</i>

58
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,695
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

59
00:04:52,592 --> 00:04:53,926
They know each other?

60
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,928
Don't ask me.

61
00:04:57,664 --> 00:05:00,500
Why a pretty lady like her?

62
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:03,202
That's Maya Kokonoe, the model, right?

63
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:05,738
I see.

64
00:05:06,673 --> 00:05:08,675
I understand the situation.

65
00:05:09,242 --> 00:05:10,777
- I'll do it.
- Will it heal?

66
00:05:12,345 --> 00:05:13,179
Yes.

67
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:16,549
But the spine is not my specialty.

68
00:05:16,616 --> 00:05:17,583
If you'd like,

69
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,686
I could introduce you
to a great doctor here.

70
00:05:19,752 --> 00:05:21,187
I said I'll do it.

71
00:05:21,254 --> 00:05:22,155
Step aside.

72
00:05:22,221 --> 00:05:23,056
Dr. Kaji,

73
00:05:23,956 --> 00:05:24,791
it has to be you.

74
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:27,593
What?

75
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:30,363
- Has to be you?
- Why?

76
00:05:31,097 --> 00:05:31,931
Me?

77
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,599
I want you to treat me.

78
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:39,072
This month's <i>Ma Qualite</i>.

79
00:05:39,138 --> 00:05:41,107
A top fashion magazine.

80
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:42,542
I know.

81
00:05:42,608 --> 00:05:43,443
How?

82
00:05:46,379 --> 00:05:50,116
"The wizard of laparoscopy
who has treated many."

83
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:51,351
"Hideki Kaji."

84
00:05:53,119 --> 00:05:55,355
We're in the same issue.

85
00:05:58,324 --> 00:06:00,927
Your specialty doesn't matter.

86
00:06:03,629 --> 00:06:04,797
This is destiny.

87
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:06,199
Destiny?

88
00:06:11,437 --> 00:06:12,505
Seriously?

89
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:15,508
With a pretty lady like her?

90
00:06:16,342 --> 00:06:17,176
This is hard.

91
00:06:20,646 --> 00:06:22,815
Yes! Beef!

92
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,050
Hold on.

93
00:06:24,117 --> 00:06:25,818
They're getting us seats.

94
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:26,853
This is great.

95
00:06:26,919 --> 00:06:28,988
- Behave yourself.
- Yeah, Michiko!

96
00:06:32,792 --> 00:06:35,128
Will Dr. Kaji operate?

97
00:06:35,194 --> 00:06:36,696
Can't decide.

98
00:06:36,763 --> 00:06:38,297
That's not like him.

99
00:06:38,364 --> 00:06:41,934
If she's a top model, the attention
and money will be great.

100
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:44,470
Something's fishy.

101
00:06:44,537 --> 00:06:46,272
What do you mean?

102
00:06:50,643 --> 00:06:51,611
Dr. Kaji?

103
00:06:52,512 --> 00:06:55,281
It's definitely fishy.

104
00:06:55,348 --> 00:06:57,717
You're right. Unbelievable.

105
00:06:57,784 --> 00:06:59,919
- Here we go.
- Sorry for the wait.

106
00:07:00,319 --> 00:07:01,287
Yes!

107
00:07:02,054 --> 00:07:03,723
Michiko, behave.

108
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:04,624
Get in line.

109
00:07:05,491 --> 00:07:06,659
I'm sorry,

110
00:07:06,726 --> 00:07:09,195
but this coupon has already expired.

111
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:10,163
EXPIRY DATE: OCTOBER 31, 2014

112
00:07:10,897 --> 00:07:12,231
Don't say that.

113
00:07:12,298 --> 00:07:13,399
We waited so long.

114
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:14,767
Mr. Hosokawa?

115
00:07:14,834 --> 00:07:19,572
- Please, let us in.
- Unbelievable. So unbelievable.

116
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,428
Sorry for the wait.

117
00:07:46,399 --> 00:07:49,435
So what did you want to talk about?

118
00:07:51,204 --> 00:07:53,272
You really don't remember me?

119
00:07:59,879 --> 00:08:01,347
Look.

120
00:08:09,722 --> 00:08:11,057
Remember now?

121
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,639
Mr. Tendo will be absent

122
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:29,442
for this week's preoperative conference.

123
00:08:30,042 --> 00:08:30,910
Therefore,

124
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:34,247
Surgical Director Fujikawa
will take his place.

125
00:08:36,215 --> 00:08:37,550
What's going on?

126
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,353
Please.

127
00:08:42,054 --> 00:08:44,390
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

128
00:08:44,457 --> 00:08:45,591
Please begin.

129
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:48,194
We will begin.

130
00:08:48,761 --> 00:08:50,863
The 1st case is Maya Kokonoe,

131
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:52,365
27 years old. Female.

132
00:08:54,567 --> 00:08:56,569
She has spinal neoplasm.

133
00:08:57,270 --> 00:09:01,007
Her kidney's left side
was removed for cancer.

134
00:09:01,073 --> 00:09:03,376
There is bone metastasis.

135
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:10,283
As requested by the patient herself,
Dr. Kaji will operate.

136
00:09:11,951 --> 00:09:12,818
What?

137
00:09:13,786 --> 00:09:15,454
Dr. Kaji, please.

138
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:23,596
Let me explain.

139
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:28,868
There is a 3cm tumor shadow
at the L3 vertebra.

140
00:09:29,368 --> 00:09:31,671
She has neuropathic pain.

141
00:09:32,104 --> 00:09:35,241
We will partially remove the vertebra

142
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:37,143
with posterior decompression.

143
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:40,379
We will also perform
frozen tumor transplant.

144
00:09:41,047 --> 00:09:43,849
The tumor will be frozen
to kill the cancer cells.

145
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:48,921
Transplanting that will increase
cancer immunity.

146
00:09:50,623 --> 00:09:51,824
Why Dr. Kaji?

147
00:09:54,727 --> 00:09:58,331
I have borrowed Dr. Fujikawa's manuscript.

148
00:10:02,668 --> 00:10:05,338
I will use this as a reference.

149
00:10:05,404 --> 00:10:06,973
Dr. Fujikawa's manuscript?

150
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,343
Did Dr. Kaji betray us?

151
00:10:12,078 --> 00:10:14,313
No way. Not Kaji.

152
00:10:14,847 --> 00:10:16,349
Feel free to use it.

153
00:10:16,749 --> 00:10:17,583
Thank you.

154
00:10:18,084 --> 00:10:18,951
I object.

155
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:26,726
Wouldn't a total resection be better?

156
00:10:26,792 --> 00:10:27,760
What?

157
00:10:27,827 --> 00:10:30,229
Total en bloc spondylectomy.

158
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:35,001
The vertebra is frozen,
placed in a titanium cage,

159
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:36,602
and returned to the spine.

160
00:10:37,103 --> 00:10:41,507
This will cure the tumor
and accomplish immunotherapy.

161
00:10:45,778 --> 00:10:47,680
That is a great method.

162
00:10:48,547 --> 00:10:49,382
Thanks.

163
00:10:49,448 --> 00:10:53,653
Kaji, how about you try her method?

164
00:10:54,053 --> 00:10:55,087
Yes, sir.

165
00:10:56,288 --> 00:10:57,123
I won't do that.

166
00:10:58,224 --> 00:10:59,291
Why?

167
00:10:59,358 --> 00:11:02,361
The patient wishes to leave in two weeks.

168
00:11:03,095 --> 00:11:06,966
Your method will take at least a month.
That's too long.

169
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:09,535
That's how it is.

170
00:11:10,736 --> 00:11:13,205
Dr. Kaji, please do your very best.

171
00:11:13,639 --> 00:11:14,473
Yes, sir.

172
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:17,943
The West's accent.

173
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,812
We will choose the assistants.

174
00:11:23,482 --> 00:11:24,684
I'll do it.

175
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,719
No, please let me.

176
00:11:26,786 --> 00:11:27,953
How simple-minded.

177
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,055
Please let me.

178
00:11:33,492 --> 00:11:35,594
Unbelievable.

179
00:11:35,661 --> 00:11:38,631
Some seem to have lewd thoughts.

180
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:40,132
What shall we do?

181
00:11:41,567 --> 00:11:44,303
I will have Dr. Daimon be the assistant.

182
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:50,776
I'm an assistant again?

183
00:12:02,254 --> 00:12:03,122
Kaji.

184
00:12:04,090 --> 00:12:04,957
Kaji.

185
00:12:07,259 --> 00:12:08,828
- Yes?
- Why are you...

186
00:12:09,328 --> 00:12:10,963
using Dr. Fujikawa's method?

187
00:12:12,264 --> 00:12:14,333
It's to meet the patient's needs.

188
00:12:15,334 --> 00:12:18,337
Did you betray the East?

189
00:12:19,772 --> 00:12:22,141
His manuscript is splendid.

190
00:12:23,476 --> 00:12:24,577
Excuse me.

191
00:12:32,318 --> 00:12:34,320
Will the East be okay?

192
00:12:38,491 --> 00:12:40,793
We will do our very best.

193
00:12:41,727 --> 00:12:43,362
Of course. You're a pro.

194
00:12:45,564 --> 00:12:47,633
This room is too dry.

195
00:12:48,033 --> 00:12:49,301
I need a humidifier.

196
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:54,173
Keep the thermos water at 40 degrees.

197
00:12:54,673 --> 00:12:57,076
I only drink 40-degree water.

198
00:12:57,476 --> 00:12:58,644
What a pain.

199
00:12:58,711 --> 00:13:00,613
And no hospital food.

200
00:13:00,679 --> 00:13:02,448
I'll choose my diet.

201
00:13:02,515 --> 00:13:03,649
No,

202
00:13:03,716 --> 00:13:06,585
we must have you follow the rules
in the hospital.

203
00:13:07,486 --> 00:13:09,255
You'll take responsibility?

204
00:13:09,321 --> 00:13:10,623
For what?

205
00:13:11,390 --> 00:13:14,727
My body's insured for 300 million yen.

206
00:13:15,094 --> 00:13:18,364
Even 1cm of fat on my belly
and my pay is halved.

207
00:13:20,566 --> 00:13:21,767
Seriously a pain.

208
00:13:23,102 --> 00:13:24,770
Please get a humidifier.

209
00:13:25,671 --> 00:13:26,505
Yes, sir.

210
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:29,308
Excuse me.

211
00:13:31,277 --> 00:13:33,212
I will bring a humidifier.

212
00:13:44,023 --> 00:13:45,191
Anything else?

213
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:51,030
Why do you want to leave in two weeks?

214
00:13:51,864 --> 00:13:53,499
Because of my schedule.

215
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:55,401
There's Paris Fashion Week.

216
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,238
You don't have to watch that.

217
00:14:01,106 --> 00:14:03,242
I'm going to be in it.

218
00:14:05,778 --> 00:14:06,612
I see.

219
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:08,881
I heard from Dr. Kaji.

220
00:14:09,481 --> 00:14:11,016
You're a part-timer?

221
00:14:11,383 --> 00:14:12,351
Freelancer.

222
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:15,955
I don't care if
the assistant's a part-timer.

223
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,325
Just be professional.

224
00:14:19,391 --> 00:14:20,960
If not, it'll be my loss.

225
00:14:23,429 --> 00:14:24,864
Yeah, yeah.

226
00:14:26,298 --> 00:14:27,166
Wait.

227
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,002
Can you get me that bag?

228
00:14:30,336 --> 00:14:31,270
My lotion's inside.

229
00:14:31,337 --> 00:14:32,571
I won't do that.

230
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,841
- What?
- I'm a professional.

231
00:14:36,508 --> 00:14:40,446
I won't do things that don't
require a medical license.

232
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,815
You piss me off.

233
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,408
I'll get an IV.

234
00:15:13,479 --> 00:15:15,080
When did you get surgery?

235
00:15:18,183 --> 00:15:19,518
Laparoscopy.

236
00:15:20,519 --> 00:15:22,221
Dr. Kaji did it, right?

237
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:25,658
Three years ago.

238
00:15:29,361 --> 00:15:31,263
When they found kidney cancer,

239
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:37,369
I was just a new, nameless model
dreaming of Fashion Week.

240
00:15:40,205 --> 00:15:43,208
It was Dr. Kaji who cured me.

241
00:15:43,642 --> 00:15:45,377
A laparoscopy expert

242
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:48,247
who received much media attention.

243
00:15:50,549 --> 00:15:51,684
Dr. Kaji

244
00:15:53,852 --> 00:15:56,155
turned my despair into hope.

245
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:59,558
But the cancer spread to your spine.

246
00:16:00,559 --> 00:16:01,393
Yes.

247
00:16:03,595 --> 00:16:04,930
I was

248
00:16:06,899 --> 00:16:08,367
once again, struck with despair.

249
00:16:13,072 --> 00:16:17,343
If he didn't get all of
the cancer that time...

250
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:24,049
It means his work wasn't professional.

251
00:16:28,587 --> 00:16:30,289
He's responsible.

252
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:40,566
So that's how you threatened Dr. Kaji.

253
00:16:42,868 --> 00:16:43,769
Of course,

254
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:46,305
I didn't give in to her threat.

255
00:16:46,372 --> 00:16:49,375
Cancer can spread
even with a perfect operation.

256
00:16:50,209 --> 00:16:53,245
The doctor shouldn't be held responsible.

257
00:16:53,312 --> 00:16:55,881
But I must get rid of the threat's cause.

258
00:16:56,448 --> 00:16:57,816
Even if I'm not at fault,

259
00:16:58,150 --> 00:17:00,486
a lawsuit would be trouble.

260
00:17:02,121 --> 00:17:04,890
Patients these days are ridiculous.

261
00:17:05,791 --> 00:17:09,361
They think they can
get paid as long as they sue.

262
00:17:09,995 --> 00:17:11,096
Exactly.

263
00:17:12,398 --> 00:17:14,066
Now the world will see my manuscript

264
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,770
with your clinical report.

265
00:17:18,637 --> 00:17:20,873
- It'd be the world's first.
- In fact...

266
00:17:21,507 --> 00:17:24,376
I was surprised
when I came across your manuscript.

267
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:28,680
What a strange turn of events.

268
00:17:28,747 --> 00:17:31,517
It means things are turning in your favor.

269
00:17:32,618 --> 00:17:35,954
If the surgery goes well,
you'll move up and get lots of money.

270
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:40,325
I'll prepare your money in cash for you.

271
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:41,727
Cash?

272
00:17:42,127 --> 00:17:43,462
Thank you.

273
00:17:44,163 --> 00:17:46,799
That's how doctors should be.

274
00:17:47,699 --> 00:17:50,035
I think we'll get along.

275
00:17:50,803 --> 00:17:52,905
A hierarchy filled with money.

276
00:17:54,006 --> 00:17:55,307
Exactly what I wish for.

277
00:17:55,374 --> 00:17:58,944
Mr. Tendo will be very happy.

278
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:10,689
How are you, Dr. Daimon?

279
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:12,825
Still a surgery machine.

280
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:15,761
I said that to show my respect.

281
00:18:15,828 --> 00:18:17,463
It wasn't an insult.

282
00:18:18,163 --> 00:18:20,566
You are truly skilled.

283
00:18:21,633 --> 00:18:24,069
But I'm an assistant now.

284
00:18:24,136 --> 00:18:28,373
You know very well about
the importance of an assistant.

285
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:31,743
You want to operate.

286
00:18:32,744 --> 00:18:35,180
I want to let you operate.

287
00:18:36,915 --> 00:18:39,017
Our interests match.

288
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:42,554
Wait.

289
00:18:45,157 --> 00:18:48,494
The beef at President Hotel isn't good.

290
00:18:50,596 --> 00:18:51,563
How'd you know?

291
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:54,566
I know a place that has good beef.

292
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:57,536
How about tonight?

293
00:19:01,406 --> 00:19:02,608
I won't do that.

294
00:19:07,679 --> 00:19:09,948
Isn't it creepy?

295
00:19:11,049 --> 00:19:12,217
It is.

296
00:19:12,284 --> 00:19:13,986
Were you followed?

297
00:19:14,052 --> 00:19:15,254
It's possible.

298
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:17,189
Maybe the robot secretary.

299
00:19:17,256 --> 00:19:18,123
Secretary?

300
00:19:18,557 --> 00:19:19,758
But why?

301
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:22,261
That president must really like you.

302
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:23,929
He likes you!

303
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:25,764
As a doctor.

304
00:19:28,066 --> 00:19:29,935
I seriously don't want that.

305
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:32,437
It's done.

306
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:36,175
Thank you for waiting.

307
00:19:36,241 --> 00:19:41,380
Now, Mai Jonouchi's brand new
2014 collection

308
00:19:41,446 --> 00:19:44,816
- will start.
- I wonder what it's like.

309
00:19:44,883 --> 00:19:46,718
- What's it like?
- I can't wait.

310
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:03,535
Nice. It looks great on you.

311
00:20:06,138 --> 00:20:09,007
Mai, you're so cute.

312
00:20:09,074 --> 00:20:11,410
That was a great job.

313
00:20:11,476 --> 00:20:13,512
I'm going to be a model.

314
00:20:14,012 --> 00:20:14,913
Well...

315
00:20:15,247 --> 00:20:18,584
Mai. Being a model is tough.

316
00:20:18,650 --> 00:20:19,718
Really?

317
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:22,221
You have to keep your figure,

318
00:20:22,287 --> 00:20:24,690
so you can't eat what you want.

319
00:20:24,756 --> 00:20:29,428
You can only drink
lukewarm 40-degree water,

320
00:20:29,828 --> 00:20:33,465
and you always need
a humidifier in your room.

321
00:20:34,366 --> 00:20:38,570
If a model slacks off for a day,
she can see it in her body.

322
00:20:38,637 --> 00:20:41,073
Two days, the cameraman can tell.

323
00:20:41,139 --> 00:20:43,609
Three days, everyone can tell.

324
00:20:43,675 --> 00:20:45,210
The two of you!

325
00:20:45,277 --> 00:20:47,279
Stop saying things
that will ruin her dream.

326
00:20:47,346 --> 00:20:48,447
Right, Mai?

327
00:20:48,513 --> 00:20:50,849
That's what a professional does.

328
00:20:51,450 --> 00:20:54,553
Michiko and Akira are too easygoing.

329
00:20:55,621 --> 00:20:57,723
Work is tough.

330
00:20:58,824 --> 00:20:59,825
Yes.

331
00:20:59,891 --> 00:21:02,327
Michiko, this is tough too.

332
00:21:02,394 --> 00:21:04,630
That one you threw away. Ron!

333
00:21:05,397 --> 00:21:07,332
8,000 points.

334
00:21:08,567 --> 00:21:09,434
I guess so.

335
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:30,188
Sorry to bother you.

336
00:21:30,522 --> 00:21:31,556
Thank you.

337
00:21:32,424 --> 00:21:33,425
Did you find it?

338
00:21:33,492 --> 00:21:35,227
Something very interesting.

339
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:36,828
MASUMI IKAWA, SECRETARY TO DR. TENDO

340
00:21:36,895 --> 00:21:39,564
CONFIDENTIAL

341
00:21:51,743 --> 00:21:54,446
The exam results for Ms. Kokonoe.

342
00:21:54,513 --> 00:21:56,315
The cancer is advanced.

343
00:21:56,381 --> 00:21:57,683
We have to hurry.

344
00:21:58,350 --> 00:21:59,651
If it gets too big,

345
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,920
a partial resection might not do it.

346
00:22:02,354 --> 00:22:03,255
Dr. Kaji.

347
00:22:04,690 --> 00:22:07,826
Thinking of changing the operative method?

348
00:22:07,893 --> 00:22:09,861
No. I won't,

349
00:22:09,928 --> 00:22:12,998
- but...
- Immunotherapy, chemo and radiotherapy.

350
00:22:13,532 --> 00:22:14,800
Things can be done later.

351
00:22:15,867 --> 00:22:16,902
I told you, right?

352
00:22:17,636 --> 00:22:20,005
My manuscript and your clinical data

353
00:22:20,072 --> 00:22:21,406
can shock the world.

354
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:24,609
Posterior decompression

355
00:22:25,143 --> 00:22:27,946
and frozen tumor transplant.

356
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:28,980
It will be called

357
00:22:29,648 --> 00:22:31,183
the Fujikawa Kaji Method.

358
00:22:31,616 --> 00:22:34,119
Fujikawa Kaji Method...

359
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:37,723
You understand the meaning of that, right?

360
00:22:41,126 --> 00:22:42,627
You're wrong.

361
00:22:43,795 --> 00:22:46,698
The Kaji Fujikawa Method.

362
00:22:48,166 --> 00:22:49,101
I'm first.

363
00:22:53,338 --> 00:22:54,706
Talking big now.

364
00:22:55,407 --> 00:22:56,308
Thank you.

365
00:22:56,375 --> 00:22:57,309
Stop that.

366
00:23:00,512 --> 00:23:02,948
PRIVATE ROOM MAYA KOKONOE

367
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,117
Excuse me.

368
00:24:12,184 --> 00:24:13,518
How could you?

369
00:24:13,585 --> 00:24:15,053
Let her.

370
00:24:36,508 --> 00:24:37,342
Are you alright?

371
00:24:41,513 --> 00:24:43,782
Yes. I can go back by myself.

372
00:24:59,464 --> 00:25:02,367
Risks include nerve root damage...

373
00:25:02,434 --> 00:25:03,735
I don't care.

374
00:25:04,503 --> 00:25:05,370
What?

375
00:25:07,973 --> 00:25:09,341
I can be in Fashion Week?

376
00:25:10,976 --> 00:25:11,810
Yes.

377
00:25:12,711 --> 00:25:14,946
Eyes around the world will be on me.

378
00:25:16,581 --> 00:25:20,418
January in Paris is for me.

379
00:25:22,854 --> 00:25:25,457
SURGERY CONSENT FORM

380
00:25:25,524 --> 00:25:27,759
SIGNED: MAYA KOKONOE

381
00:25:33,665 --> 00:25:34,799
Don't fail this time.

382
00:25:37,168 --> 00:25:41,139
I...never failed.

383
00:25:54,786 --> 00:25:55,854
Good, right?

384
00:25:55,921 --> 00:25:56,788
What do you want?

385
00:25:57,923 --> 00:26:01,026
You think I failed in her surgery before?

386
00:26:01,092 --> 00:26:02,627
- You did?
- Idiot.

387
00:26:03,128 --> 00:26:05,730
The wizard makes no mistakes.

388
00:26:05,797 --> 00:26:07,098
Really?

389
00:26:07,165 --> 00:26:08,767
Patients always blame the doctor

390
00:26:08,833 --> 00:26:10,435
if they get sick again.

391
00:26:10,502 --> 00:26:13,038
Give me a break!

392
00:26:14,105 --> 00:26:16,808
Whether the cancer spreads or not is luck.

393
00:26:18,977 --> 00:26:20,779
It's inevitable.

394
00:26:20,845 --> 00:26:21,713
Exactly.

395
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:23,882
So it's not your fault.

396
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:24,950
Of course.

397
00:26:25,850 --> 00:26:27,752
I've seen thousands of patients.

398
00:26:27,819 --> 00:26:29,588
I can't remember them all.

399
00:26:31,156 --> 00:26:32,157
Really?

400
00:26:33,158 --> 00:26:34,259
I do.

401
00:26:34,326 --> 00:26:35,727
Seriously?

402
00:26:36,728 --> 00:26:40,432
For you, that patient might be
one out of many.

403
00:26:41,299 --> 00:26:43,768
For the patient, you're the only doctor.

404
00:26:46,404 --> 00:26:47,772
It makes me sick.

405
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:52,043
- What does?
- Skewers and doctors like you.

406
00:26:52,677 --> 00:26:56,381
Like me? And you don't like skewers?
Want to go somewhere else?

407
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:00,018
I won't do that.

408
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,158
But...

409
00:27:09,260 --> 00:27:11,429
She ate a lot.

410
00:27:28,446 --> 00:27:29,314
Good morning.

411
00:27:30,815 --> 00:27:33,952
Today's surgery is a world's first.

412
00:27:34,919 --> 00:27:35,987
Good luck.

413
00:27:36,454 --> 00:27:37,288
Yes, sir.

414
00:27:49,801 --> 00:27:53,638
Partial vertebra resection
with posterior decompression

415
00:27:53,705 --> 00:27:56,174
and frozen tumor transplant.

416
00:27:56,241 --> 00:27:57,075
Please begin.

417
00:27:57,609 --> 00:27:58,576
Let's begin.

418
00:27:58,643 --> 00:28:01,780
Blood pressure 80, pulse 60 and sinus.

419
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:03,181
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

420
00:28:06,217 --> 00:28:07,318
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

421
00:28:18,396 --> 00:28:19,230
- Retractor.
- Yes.

422
00:28:22,567 --> 00:28:23,835
Where's Mr. Tendo?

423
00:28:23,902 --> 00:28:25,370
He's out again.

424
00:28:25,437 --> 00:28:28,540
A crucial moment for the new bill.

425
00:28:28,606 --> 00:28:30,008
I'm sure he's busy.

426
00:28:30,775 --> 00:28:32,911
We must have a world's first case

427
00:28:33,344 --> 00:28:35,880
and support the president.

428
00:28:35,947 --> 00:28:38,016
Good luck, Dr. Kaji.

429
00:28:38,083 --> 00:28:41,119
This hospital will become world-renowned.

430
00:28:41,186 --> 00:28:42,153
That's right.

431
00:28:44,589 --> 00:28:47,258
You're not going
to watch Dr. Kaji's operation?

432
00:28:48,960 --> 00:28:51,663
I have my pride as the head of the East.

433
00:28:53,631 --> 00:28:54,599
Have you no pride?

434
00:28:58,803 --> 00:28:59,637
Hara?

435
00:29:03,341 --> 00:29:04,909
Maybe I'll go to the West.

436
00:29:04,976 --> 00:29:06,578
KIYOSHIRO FUJIKAWA, SURGICAL DIRECTOR

437
00:29:06,644 --> 00:29:08,646
TOMOKO SEKIGAHARA, SECRETARY

438
00:29:19,624 --> 00:29:21,926
Be careful scraping the outer tumor.

439
00:29:22,794 --> 00:29:23,661
I know.

440
00:29:24,863 --> 00:29:26,097
- Kerrison punch.
- Yes.

441
00:29:37,008 --> 00:29:38,510
I see the nerve root.

442
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:47,285
Invasion of the centrum is bad.

443
00:29:48,386 --> 00:29:51,556
A partial resection
can't get the whole tumor.

444
00:29:52,423 --> 00:29:55,393
Neither will a frozen tumor transplant.

445
00:30:06,137 --> 00:30:07,605
Total resection.

446
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:11,042
Then she can't leave in 2 weeks.

447
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:14,012
Our job's to answer her needs.

448
00:30:14,078 --> 00:30:16,347
Want her to say you failed again?

449
00:30:22,520 --> 00:30:24,689
Want her to say you failed again?

450
00:30:27,959 --> 00:30:29,160
What are you doing?

451
00:30:29,894 --> 00:30:31,129
Hurry up.

452
00:30:31,196 --> 00:30:33,798
Kaji, do it with my method.

453
00:30:33,865 --> 00:30:35,567
Continue the operation.

454
00:30:38,169 --> 00:30:41,239
Or do you not want
your bosses to say you failed?

455
00:30:45,610 --> 00:30:48,179
Who is the surgery for, moron?

456
00:30:53,585 --> 00:30:54,586
Well?

457
00:30:57,555 --> 00:30:59,591
Your directions, please.

458
00:31:10,768 --> 00:31:12,036
Don't fail this time.

459
00:31:27,619 --> 00:31:29,454
Change to Dr. Daimon's method.

460
00:31:30,922 --> 00:31:32,056
What?

461
00:31:33,191 --> 00:31:34,893
- Yes.
- Nurse.

462
00:31:34,959 --> 00:31:36,561
- Get a titanium cage.
- Yes.

463
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:41,599
Daimon, it's your method.

464
00:31:41,666 --> 00:31:42,767
You do it.

465
00:31:43,701 --> 00:31:45,937
Damn you! Changing the method?

466
00:31:46,004 --> 00:31:48,106
Making her responsible?

467
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:51,242
The part-timer's method will fail.

468
00:31:52,477 --> 00:31:55,179
My method doesn't fail.

469
00:31:55,613 --> 00:31:56,748
My goodness.

470
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:04,589
Let's switch.

471
00:32:04,656 --> 00:32:05,890
I won't do that.

472
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:11,162
Why not?

473
00:32:12,330 --> 00:32:13,798
I told you.

474
00:32:14,132 --> 00:32:16,601
For her, you're the only doctor.

475
00:32:19,337 --> 00:32:21,172
You're a pro, right?

476
00:32:30,348 --> 00:32:32,717
How cool.

477
00:32:34,152 --> 00:32:36,721
And I even offered you my spot.

478
00:32:43,027 --> 00:32:44,462
We will now change to

479
00:32:44,529 --> 00:32:47,365
total en bloc spondylectomy.

480
00:32:47,732 --> 00:32:48,599
Yes.

481
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:52,170
Here's the cage.

482
00:32:52,236 --> 00:32:53,504
Let's begin.

483
00:32:58,109 --> 00:32:59,877
Separate the vertebra.

484
00:32:59,944 --> 00:33:01,012
- Kelly forceps.
- Yes.

485
00:33:01,079 --> 00:33:03,514
Somatic artery branch ligation.

486
00:33:03,581 --> 00:33:04,549
- Pean.
- Yes.

487
00:33:11,689 --> 00:33:13,891
Kaji!

488
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:19,897
- Metzenbaum.
- Yes.

489
00:33:22,100 --> 00:33:24,535
We will separate the centrum.

490
00:33:24,602 --> 00:33:25,603
- Gigli saw.
- Yes.

491
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,239
- Clamp.
- Yes.

492
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:44,022
Freeze the vertebra with liquid nitrogen.

493
00:33:52,230 --> 00:33:54,632
- 20 minutes.
- Measuring time.

494
00:33:54,699 --> 00:33:57,468
Crush and pack into the cage.

495
00:33:57,535 --> 00:33:58,903
Got it.

496
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:12,817
The cage has been set.

497
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:15,620
Now just stabilize.

498
00:34:15,686 --> 00:34:16,521
- Scissors.
- Yes.

499
00:34:18,356 --> 00:34:20,124
- Get the probe ready too.
- Yes.

500
00:34:23,261 --> 00:34:25,530
SURGERY TIME

501
00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:33,604
Finished.

502
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:35,339
Thank you.

503
00:34:35,940 --> 00:34:37,108
Thank you.

504
00:34:37,775 --> 00:34:39,677
Thank you so much.

505
00:34:40,878 --> 00:34:42,847
I should've never met you.

506
00:34:44,081 --> 00:34:46,584
You're a Demon until the very end.

507
00:34:49,053 --> 00:34:50,054
What?

508
00:34:54,025 --> 00:34:54,926
Demon.

509
00:35:20,551 --> 00:35:23,488
Because of you,
a world's first is no more.

510
00:35:25,256 --> 00:35:28,626
You've embarrassed Mr. Tendo.

511
00:35:30,761 --> 00:35:32,263
Who cares?

512
00:35:38,002 --> 00:35:39,303
You'll pay for this.

513
00:35:42,373 --> 00:35:44,008
I'm ready.

514
00:36:08,733 --> 00:36:09,567
Kaji.

515
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:21,379
Thank you for everything.

516
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:27,752
Dr. Kaji.

517
00:36:29,053 --> 00:36:34,458
Come back!

518
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,431
What's this?

519
00:36:41,532 --> 00:36:43,301
A cowboy movie?

520
00:36:48,239 --> 00:36:51,475
I heard you changed
the method during surgery.

521
00:36:53,544 --> 00:36:54,712
I apologize.

522
00:36:55,079 --> 00:36:57,281
A doctor like you

523
00:36:57,715 --> 00:36:59,617
teaming up with a part-timer?

524
00:37:07,592 --> 00:37:08,426
Please.

525
00:37:08,492 --> 00:37:10,394
RESIGNATION

526
00:37:15,099 --> 00:37:16,067
Dr. Kaji.

527
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:21,005
Shouldn't you be
turning in a clinical report

528
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:24,175
instead of a resignation?

529
00:37:27,645 --> 00:37:31,616
Total en bloc spondylectomy.

530
00:37:32,383 --> 00:37:35,620
There have not been many reports of this.

531
00:37:35,686 --> 00:37:42,159
That is what we must
transmit to the world from our hospital.

532
00:37:49,500 --> 00:37:52,370
I will write a clinical report right away.

533
00:37:54,672 --> 00:37:55,506
Please do.

534
00:37:55,873 --> 00:37:56,707
Yes.

535
00:37:59,010 --> 00:38:00,077
Excuse me.

536
00:38:00,144 --> 00:38:01,112
You again!

537
00:38:01,178 --> 00:38:03,714
Dr. Kaji. Good to see you again.

538
00:38:05,182 --> 00:38:09,787
Thank you for using
our Daimon and Jonouchi.

539
00:38:11,188 --> 00:38:12,123
This is a melon.

540
00:38:14,792 --> 00:38:16,093
This is a bill.

541
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:24,201
Excuse me.

542
00:38:24,268 --> 00:38:25,903
- What?
- 10 million yen?

543
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:29,473
What is this
absolutely preposterous price?

544
00:38:32,443 --> 00:38:34,078
We cannot accept this.

545
00:38:34,645 --> 00:38:35,813
Excuse me?

546
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:38,616
Dr. Kaji was the surgeon.

547
00:38:39,083 --> 00:38:41,118
Dr. Daimon was an assistant.

548
00:38:41,185 --> 00:38:42,920
That's exactly right.

549
00:38:42,987 --> 00:38:43,854
However,

550
00:38:43,921 --> 00:38:46,057
if Dr. Daimon weren't there,

551
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:51,262
Dr. Kaji would've
followed Dr. Fujikawa's method.

552
00:38:52,463 --> 00:38:55,599
If so, a cancer that would be incurable

553
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:59,437
with immunotherapy would've remained.

554
00:38:59,503 --> 00:39:02,506
This could've developed into

555
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:06,911
an ugly medical lawsuit that sees no end.

556
00:39:08,346 --> 00:39:10,147
If you think about the trial costs,

557
00:39:10,948 --> 00:39:12,550
this price is

558
00:39:12,616 --> 00:39:18,122
extremely fair and reasonable.

559
00:39:19,223 --> 00:39:20,057
So as usual,

560
00:39:20,124 --> 00:39:23,294
we will wire the money to your account.

561
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,664
Thank you.

562
00:39:28,766 --> 00:39:31,802
By the way,
who should I give the melon to?

563
00:39:52,456 --> 00:39:54,125
Oh well.

564
00:39:56,660 --> 00:39:59,263
I haven't skipped in a while.

565
00:39:59,630 --> 00:40:01,365
About Dr. Daimon's payment...

566
00:40:01,432 --> 00:40:03,934
About doubling her contract money?

567
00:40:04,535 --> 00:40:07,938
That's how greatly she contributes here.

568
00:40:08,005 --> 00:40:09,573
I did that.

569
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:12,443
No, it's about the fee
we pay her each time.

570
00:40:13,310 --> 00:40:15,913
It's over 100 million yen now.

571
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:16,981
And?

572
00:40:17,047 --> 00:40:19,617
It's not the hospital account,

573
00:40:19,683 --> 00:40:22,720
so where is the money coming from?

574
00:40:22,787 --> 00:40:24,789
It's not the hospital's money.

575
00:40:30,728 --> 00:40:34,465
Need I explain further?

576
00:40:36,133 --> 00:40:36,967
No!

577
00:40:45,943 --> 00:40:46,844
My stomach hurts.

578
00:40:49,814 --> 00:40:50,881
Hang in there.

579
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:53,451
Yes, ma'am.

580
00:40:57,221 --> 00:40:58,522
Nice restaurant.

581
00:40:59,056 --> 00:41:02,193
I'm glad you like it.

582
00:41:02,259 --> 00:41:03,561
The wine list.

583
00:41:03,627 --> 00:41:04,495
Water is fine.

584
00:41:05,696 --> 00:41:06,530
Certainly.

585
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:13,003
Did you hear that

586
00:41:13,571 --> 00:41:16,273
I'll be the next Minister of
Health, Labor and Welfare?

587
00:41:18,375 --> 00:41:22,146
So much attention
just because I'm a woman.

588
00:41:22,213 --> 00:41:27,418
The Prime Minister chose you
for your abilities, Ms. Tokachi.

589
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:29,653
You sure are good.

590
00:41:31,222 --> 00:41:32,056
Mr. Tendo.

591
00:41:32,990 --> 00:41:35,259
It seems you're going around
other ministries

592
00:41:35,759 --> 00:41:38,796
to get them on your side.

593
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:41,999
I've paid my respects, yes.

594
00:41:42,066 --> 00:41:44,068
Your plans for...

595
00:41:45,369 --> 00:41:50,007
The Japan Healthcare Organization, was it?

596
00:41:50,941 --> 00:41:51,775
Yes.

597
00:41:52,209 --> 00:41:55,279
It's too hard. I don't get it.

598
00:41:56,413 --> 00:41:57,948
I'm against it.

599
00:42:00,618 --> 00:42:01,519
I'm sorry.

600
00:42:04,388 --> 00:42:06,423
Dinner is over.

601
00:42:07,291 --> 00:42:08,125
Excuse me.

602
00:42:11,295 --> 00:42:12,463
Please wait.

603
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:18,602
I still have something
important to talk about.

604
00:42:27,144 --> 00:42:28,479
Things are going well.

605
00:42:30,281 --> 00:42:31,815
I don't care anymore.

606
00:42:36,287 --> 00:42:38,255
I can't leave in two weeks, right?

607
00:42:40,357 --> 00:42:41,191
No.

608
00:42:41,992 --> 00:42:46,063
In the end, you couldn't
answer my request.

609
00:42:49,133 --> 00:42:50,200
You failed.

610
00:42:53,370 --> 00:42:54,271
I'm sorry.

611
00:42:55,873 --> 00:42:58,042
You're apologizing?

612
00:43:00,844 --> 00:43:01,845
You know,

613
00:43:02,613 --> 00:43:04,882
because he didn't fail,

614
00:43:04,949 --> 00:43:06,817
you can keep on living.

615
00:43:08,852 --> 00:43:09,687
Daimon.

616
00:43:10,387 --> 00:43:12,856
Besides, you keep
talking about Fashion Week,

617
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:14,425
as if it's something incredible,

618
00:43:14,925 --> 00:43:16,393
but all you do is walk, right?

619
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:19,396
You can do that whenever.

620
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:24,034
Bye.

621
00:43:31,942 --> 00:43:32,776
That woman

622
00:43:33,611 --> 00:43:34,645
really pisses me off.

623
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:38,015
I understand.

624
00:43:39,483 --> 00:43:42,252
That woman is a demon who angers people.

625
00:43:46,991 --> 00:43:48,025
Thanks.

626
00:43:51,462 --> 00:43:53,197
I'll invite you to Fashion Week.

627
00:44:00,571 --> 00:44:01,405
Please do.

628
00:44:13,050 --> 00:44:16,654
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

629
00:44:17,054 --> 00:44:21,291
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

630
00:44:21,358 --> 00:44:22,226
Not bad.

631
00:44:29,433 --> 00:44:30,834
It's hard.

632
00:44:30,901 --> 00:44:32,636
We're fine now.

633
00:44:32,703 --> 00:44:36,974
I made sure
those four coupons aren't expired.

634
00:44:37,041 --> 00:44:38,275
Isn't this nice?

635
00:44:38,342 --> 00:44:40,144
Yes!

636
00:44:40,210 --> 00:44:41,879
I'm sorry,

637
00:44:41,945 --> 00:44:45,315
but you can only use two coupons at once.

638
00:44:47,051 --> 00:44:48,752
Rock, paper, scissors.

639
00:44:49,253 --> 00:44:50,621
Yes!

640
00:44:51,088 --> 00:44:52,956
Oh no!

641
00:44:53,023 --> 00:44:53,991
Let's go, Mai.

642
00:44:54,825 --> 00:44:55,893
Behave yourself.

643
00:44:57,227 --> 00:45:00,264
I want beef.

644
00:45:00,330 --> 00:45:03,133
- Akira, I want beef!
- You're so loud!

645
00:45:06,270 --> 00:45:07,137
Am I...

646
00:45:09,039 --> 00:45:10,441
Fired?

647
00:45:18,716 --> 00:45:19,983
The next patient.

648
00:45:25,789 --> 00:45:30,194
Large hepatocellular carcinoma
with myocardial infarction.

649
00:45:30,694 --> 00:45:36,300
A massive 13cm tumor
has been located on the liver.

650
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:40,504
A case that matches your manuscript.

651
00:45:42,740 --> 00:45:43,774
Let me take a look.

652
00:45:50,013 --> 00:45:53,050
YOSHIKO TOKACHI

653
00:45:53,117 --> 00:45:55,219
It's your last chance.

654
00:45:56,653 --> 00:46:00,824
Next time, you must get a world's
first case with your manuscript...

655
00:46:03,594 --> 00:46:06,130
...using Michiko Daimon.

656
00:46:12,102 --> 00:46:12,936
Yes, sir.

657
00:46:25,382 --> 00:46:26,216
Do you...

658
00:46:28,051 --> 00:46:29,353
work at this hospital?

659
00:46:30,320 --> 00:46:31,321
Yes.

660
00:46:32,623 --> 00:46:34,491
Do you know Doctor-X?

661
00:46:41,532 --> 00:46:44,168
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

662
00:46:44,234 --> 00:46:45,402
<i>also known as</i>

663
00:46:45,903 --> 00:46:47,838
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

664
00:46:49,006 --> 00:46:52,009
Everything you say sounds fake.

665
00:46:52,075 --> 00:46:53,310
What?

666
00:46:53,377 --> 00:46:55,813
I won't assist factional disputes.

667
00:46:55,879 --> 00:46:57,481
I won't forgive you.

668
00:46:57,548 --> 00:46:58,782
Your fault!

669
00:46:58,849 --> 00:47:00,050
Too sloppy.

670
00:47:00,117 --> 00:47:02,419
You're no longer my teacher.

671
00:47:02,486 --> 00:47:03,887
Don't order me.
